<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Vencemos started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Vencemos started.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santander Investment analyst Guillermo Serrano started coverage of Venezuelan cement company Vencemos SA Thursday with a rating of market perform.</p>
<p>-- In a report, Serrano said he expected earnings per share equivalent to $0.22 and $0.21 for 1997 and 1998, respectively. Last year, the company reported earnings of $0.18 a share.</p>
<p>-- The 12-month target price equivalent to $2.50 a share implies a 25 percent rise in dollar terms.</p>
<p>-- The company's shares were off five bolivares to 1,035 bolivares in Caracas.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
